  "raw": {
    "https://www.inter.edu/en/meet-us-at/jobs-3/": {
      "title": "Careers - Inter-American University of Puerto Rico",
      "description": "Careers - Inter-American University of Puerto Rico Skip to content +1 (787) 766-1912 Search UKG Blackboard Professional Licensure Inter Web E-mail Apply for Admission Accessibility / Accessibility Español MENU Search Institution Close Institution Open Institution Home Get to know us Mission and Vision University goals University governance Accreditations Board of Trustees President University Council Institutional Office of Academic Research Jobs News Enclosures Academic Offering Close Academic Offering Open Academic Offering Introduction Technical Certificates Associate Degrees Baccalaureates Masters Doctorates Optometry School Faculty of Law Admissions Financial Assistance Close Financial Aid Open Financial Aid Introduction Scholarships Private Scholarships Loans Study and Work Cost of Education (COA) Calendar of Events Financial Assistance Services to Servicemen, Veterans and their Dependents Student Life Close Student Life Open Student Life Introduction Exchange Opportunities Sports Services Information Access Center Professional Counseling Services to students with disabilities Blackboard InterWeb Documents Close Documents Open Documents Documents CARES ACT 2020 - 2022 REPORTS Online Catalogs Gainful Employment Multi-factor Authentication (MFA) User's Guide Academic Calendars Restart of Classes Protocol Cost Bulletins Link to submit Financial Assistance documents CECIA CDPEE HETS Professional Licensure Notifications Virtual Chaplaincy Development and Alumni Jobs Get to know us Mission and Vision University Goals Accreditations University Government Board of Trustees University Council Institutional Office of Academic Research Jobs Documents We provide a positive work environment, continuous learning and deep respect for the dignity of each employee. To learn more about the details of each call, click on the links below. IMPORTANT All applications for employment must be accompanied by a resume, academic credentials and the two self-identification forms for veterans and people with disabilities that are available on our DOCUMENTS Keywords Location Daytime Irregular Full Day Part-time Nocturno RSS Your browser does not support JavaScript, or it is disabled. JavaScript must be enabled in order to view listings. Assistant Dean Aguadilla Campus Posted 1 day ago Teacher San German Campus Posted 5 days ago Técnico de Laboratorio de Ciencias (Enfermería) Bayamon Campus Posted 6 days ago Director of Information Systems Fajardo Campus Posted 6 days ago Conservation and Maintenance Manager Bayamon Campus Posted 1 week ago Counselor Arecibo Campus Posted 1 week ago Director of Financial Aid Ponce Campus Posted 1 week ago Executive Assistant I System Central Office Posted 1 week ago Associate Dean San German Campus Posted 1 week ago Research Technician Ponce Campus Posted 1 week ago Load more listings Inter-American University The Inter-American University of Puerto Rico is a private, non-profit institution of higher education with deep Christian roots. Accreditations LINKS OF INTEREST Professional Licensure Notifications Share Facebook X Twitter Linkedin Whatsapp The Universidad Interamericana de Puerto Rico (UIPR) holds a Renewal License from the Puerto Rico Board of Postsecondary Institutions and all academic programs, including online education programs, are authorized by the Agency. UIPR is an accredited institution and a member of the Middle States Commission on Higher Education (MSCHE) www.msche.org . The accreditation status of the Inter-American University of Puerto Rico is “Reaffirmed Accreditation”. The Commission's most recent action on the accreditation status of the Institution on June 22, 2023 was to reaffirm the accreditation status. MSCHE is recognized by the U.S. Secretary of Education to conduct accreditation and pre-accreditation (candidate status) activities for institutions of higher education, including distance education, correspondence, and direct assessment programs offered at such institutions. The geographic area of the Commission's accreditation activities extends throughout the United States. The Institution is approved by the State Veterans Educational Services Agency to provide academic training to students under various GI Bill® programs. GI Bill® is a registered trademark of the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA). The Inter-American University of Puerto Rico has a process for its students to file complaints when they believe their rights have been affected. Once submitted, the complaint will be handled in accordance with the General Student Regulations , Chapter II - Rights and Duties of Students. Use the form available in the Online Academic and Student Support Center to submit a complaint or claim. The Inter American University of Puerto Rico provides a process through which a student who considers that their rights have been affected may address complaints and grievances. After the student submits a claim, their grievance will be addressed in accordance with the General Student Regulations , Chapter II, Student Rights and Duties. To file a complaint or claim, please access the form within our Online Center for Academic and Student Support. This English version of the website has been automatically translated for your convenience. We are currently reviewing and revising the content through a human editing process to ensure accuracy, clarity, and consistency. We appreciate your patience during this transition and welcome any feedback if you notice areas that may need clarification."
    },
    "https://www.inter.edu/job_listing/decanoa-auxiliar-14/": {
      "title": "Decano(a) Auxiliar",
      "description": "Decano(a) Auxiliar – Universidad Interamericana de Puerto Rico Ir al contenido +1 (787) 766-1912 Búsqueda UKG Blackboard Licencia Profesional Inter Web Correo Electrónico Solicita Admisión Accesibilidad / Accessibility English MENÚ Búsqueda Institución Cerrar Institución Abrir Institución Inicio Conócenos Misión y Visión Metas de la universidad Gobierno universitario Acreditaciones Junta de Síndicos Presidenta Consejo Universitario Oficina Institucional de Investigación Académica Empleos Noticias Recintos Oferta Académica Cerrar Oferta Académica Abrir Oferta Académica Introducción Certificados Técnicos Grados Asociados Bachilleratos Maestrías Doctorados Escuela de Optometría Facultad de Derecho Admisiones Ayudas Económicas Cerrar Ayudas Económicas Abrir Ayudas Económicas Introducción Becas Becas Privadas Préstamos Estudio y Trabajo Costo de Educación (COA) Calendario Eventos Asistencia Económica Servicios a Militares, Veteranos y sus Dependientes Vida Estudiantil Cerrar Vida Estudiantil Abrir Vida Estudiantil Introducción Oportunidades de Intercambio Deportes Servicios Centro de Acceso a la Información Consejería Profesional Servicios al estudiante con discapacidades Blackboard InterWeb Documentos Cerrar Documentos Abrir Documentos Documentos INFORMES CARES ACT 2020 – 2022 Catálogos en línea Gainful Employment Multi-factor Authentication (MFA) Guía de usuario Calendarios Académicos Protocolo Reinicio de Clases Boletines de Costos Enlace para enviar documentos de Asistencia Económica CECIA CDPEE HETS Professional Licensure Notifications Capellanía Virtual Desarrollo y Exalumnos Decano(a) Auxiliar Recinto de Aguadilla Publicado hace 23 horas Decano_Aux_003544 Universidad Interamericana La Universidad Interamericana de Puerto Rico es una institución privada, de educación superior con profundas raíces cristianas, sin fines de lucro. Acreditaciones ENLACES DE INTERÉS Professional Licensure Notifications Compartir Facebook X Twitter Linkedin Whatsapp La Universidad Interamericana de Puerto Rico (UIPR) posee Licencia de Renovación de la Junta de Instituciones Postsecundarias de Puerto Rico y todos los programas académicos, incluyendo los programas de educación en línea, están autorizados por dicha Agencia. La UIPR es una institución acreditada y miembro de la Middle States Commission on Higher Education (MSCHE) www.msche.org . El estatus de acreditación de la Universidad Interamericana de Puerto Rico es “Acreditación Reafirmada”. La acción más reciente de la Comisión sobre el estatus de acreditación de la Institución el 22 de junio de 2023 fue reafirmar el estatus de acreditación. La MSCHE está reconocida por la Secretaría de Educación de los Estados Unidos para llevar a cabo actividades de acreditación y preacreditación (estatus de candidato) para instituciones de educación superior, incluyendo educación a distancia, por correspondencia y programas de evaluación directa ofrecidos en dichas instituciones. El área geográfica de las actividades de acreditación de la Comisión se extiende por todo Estados Unidos. La Institución está aprobada por la Agencia Estatal de Servicios Educativos a Veteranos para proveer formación académica a los estudiantes bajo diversos programas GI Bill®. GI Bill® es una marca registrada del Departamento de Asuntos al Veterano (VA). La Universidad Interamericana de Puerto Rico cuenta con un proceso para que sus estudiantes presenten sus reclamaciones cuando entienden que sus derechos han sido afectados. Una vez sometida, la reclamación será atendida en conformidad con el Reglamento General de Estudiantes , Capítulo II – Derechos y deberes de los estudiantes. Utilice el formulario disponible en el Centro de Apoyo Académico y Estudiantil en Línea para someter una querella o reclamación. The Inter American University of Puerto Rico provides a process through which a student who considers that their rights have been affected may address complaints and grievances. After the student submits a claim, their grievance will be addressed in accordance with the General Student Regulations , Chapter II, Student Rights and Duties. To file a complaint or claim, please access the form within our Online Center for Academic and Student Support."
    },
